We’re a large and growing professional services firm that still feels like a community. With over 76,000 professionals in more than 150 countries, we combine global scale with local expertise to help dynamic organizations unlock their potential for growth. We truly care about our colleagues, our clients, and the communities where we work and live.




 As Assistant Manager in the FCC Advisory practice, you will support high\-quality client engagements to assess and enhance FCC systems and controls. You will support the engagement manager with the overall project, supporting the project teams under the oversight of the Engagement Partner/Engagement Director, ensuring successful delivery of complex and diverse engagements, while collaborating with leadership and cross\-functional teams. You are “hands\-on” and possess a robust understanding of the overall FCC Framework, with the ability to apply this knowledge to the various client needs to ensure high quality project delivery with practical, implementable solutions for our clients. Discover your purple and join our Regulatory \& Financial Crime Compliance team today!




**Let us paint a picture for you**
 Imagine being part of a team that puts “we before me”, where flexibility is a mindset, and where you trust your colleagues to have your back.




 Imagine working for an organization that believes in the power of authenticity in everything that we do. Whether you're steering discussions in a client meeting, tackling your fear of heights at the top of the Burj Khalifa or ziplining across Jebel Jais – bring your true self to work. Be a part of a team driven by a purpose of shaping the world that we live in, based on trust and integrity in markets, dynamic businesses, and communities where businesses and people thrive.




 Join us to expand your horizons, be inspired, face challenges, and most importantly, be yourself.




**About the FCC Advisory Practice**
 The teams services focus on assurance / independent FCC Program assessments / third party validation and monitorships, and AML Program development, uplift and remediation, including design and implementation of (key elements) of firms ’ FCC Programs (such as Financial Crime Risk Assessments, Policies \& Procedures development, Target Operating Model design). We also support clients with FCC technology needs, such as independent validation of TM \& Sanctions systems, effectiveness testing and optimization and support in the vendor selection and implementation phase.




**As an Assistant Manager some of your responsibilities will include:**
* Delivery: Be the execution lead for smaller client engagements or support workstreams on medium/large scale projects under the oversight of the Project Lead, Engagement Partner/Engagement Director. These projects may include:






 o   Assurance / Independent FCC assessments:




 o   Performing AML Program Assessment, Internal Audits;




 o   Conducting gap analysis;




 o   Executing Agreed Upon Procedures (AUPs); and




 o   Participating in Third Party Validation / Monitorship




* AML Program development and uplift:






 o   Supporting with the development and execution of key elements of firms’ FCC Programs for example FCC risk assessments and Risk Appetite Statement, FCC policies and procedures, Transaction Monitoring Typology Assessments, \& Customer Risk Assessment Models under the guidance and with the oversight of the Project Lead




* Project Management:






 o   Supporting the planning, execution, and delivery of projects, including client updates, progress tracking, billing, and quality assurance




 o   Overseeing project engagement formalities, such as conflict checks, client acceptance, and documentation




* Business \& Practice Development:






 o   Driving business development activities, including preparing proposals, marketing efforts, and thought leadership




 o   Actively participating in client pitches, providing strategic insights and solutions




 o   Supervising junior team members to ensure high\-quality outputs




 o   Contributing to internal knowledge sharing




**Think you've got what it takes to be an Assistant Manager? Like the color purple? Great. Here's a few more boxes we're also hoping you can tick:**
* 5\+ years of experience working in Financial Crime Advisory (Consulting) and/or in financial institutions (2nd Line of Defence with advisory type responsibilities);
* Very good practical understanding of the key elements of a robust FCC Program;
* Understanding of Financial Crime Systems I.e. Transaction Monitoring and Sanctions Screening;
* Proficient in drafting policies and procedures related to FCC;
* Familiarity of regulatory requirements and expectation for AML/CFT, CPF and Sanctions in the UAE 
 **OR** 
  other key international jurisdictions (such as UK, EU, Singapore, Hong Kong, etc.);
* Proven track record of leading the execution of small AML Advisory projects and/supporting key workstreams on medium/large scale projects;
* Strong and demonstrated project and stakeholder management skills;
* Strong and demonstrated Business Development skills with regard to proposal development, thought leadership;
* Excellent communication skills in both written and spoken English;
* Excellent interpersonal skills – with positive \& enthusiastic attitude;
* Ability to thrive in a multi\-cultural environment;
* Strong proficiency in Microsoft office applications; and
* A critical thinker with a strong eye for detail and creative in problem solving, strong analytical skills.


 Advantageous but not a requirement:
* Hold a leading professional qualification such as CAMS, ICA, CFE or similar professional certifications;
* Knowledge of other financial crime legislation/regulation (e.g., Anti\-Bribery \& Corruption, Fraud, Market Abuse) is advantageous but not required
* Excellent communication skills in both written and spoken Arabic is advantageous






 .

The role is responsible for discharging Project Management activities across the Qatar In\-Service Typhoon Availability Service Operation at Dukhan Airbase, Qatar, as CAM133\. This role will undertake Project Management activities within the respective technical delivery areas to ensure key PM tenets are discharged and upheld.




 The incumbent will be required to gather, synthesize \& integrate information relating to performance (cost, resources and outputs), generate, monitor and report progress against plans, identify trends, analyze and interpret data and information to ensure all data and information is accurate, generate and publish regular reports, including internal contract review packs and external customer facing material




 This role will be geographically deployed out into the respective delivery area, providing a Project Management service into the allocated area. Hierarchically, this role will report into the Project Management Lead, who will provide support, leadership and the PM governance framework the incumbent will be required to operate within.




 The role will also be required to support and conduct any ad\-hoc PM activities required due to the nature of Operations at Dukhan Airbase.




**Project Management**
* Provide deployed Project Management support to Dukhan Delivery areas
* Run a subset of the Dukhan Business Rhythm within each delivery area, ensuring Risk, Opportunity, Change (Organisational or Technical) and Spend are reviewed within each team
* Co\-ordinate, facilitate and compile agreed OPR inputs on behalf of each delivery area
* Act as the deployed Project Management conscience of the Dukhan Operation, ensuring delivery areas remain within governance, escalating issues as required.
* Operate as ‘critical friends’ of the deployed areas, providing a valued Project Management service whilst driving and upholding PM values and standards
* Support compilation of PM\&C artefacts into the drumbeat Dukhan SMT Business Rhythm reviews (for example, Change Requests)
* Champion Continuous Improvement initiatives into the CI lead, seeking to maximise operational efficiency and minimising costs;
* Responsible for managing the financial information for the allocated area, to feed the Contract Status Reports (CSR);
* Responsible for managing the Risk and Opportunities (financial, quality, scope and quality) within the allocated area
* Develop, manage and maintain integrated program schedules for non\-recurring elements of wor
* Manage and measure delivery against the contract, advising on contractual compliance / shortfalls for both BAES and the QEAF (BFP/R)
* Co\-ordinate, control and report against internal and contractual KPI’s
* Act as an interface with junior officers within the QEAF for the allocated area for all applicable Project Delivery requirements
* Responsible for managing the resource manpower within the allocated area from a PM standpoint (e.g. cost, resource planning, capacity modelling)
* Support reviews (preparation or attendance) including but not limited to OPR, QCRs, QBRs, risk \& opportunity, Change Control Boards, Business Operations and customer PRMs;
* Provide support to the Business Management Lead for control of the Resource management aspects of the Typhoon Availability Service


**Additional Responsibilities / Activities**
* Ensure compliance with the mandated BAE Systems Governance Framework, including, but not limited to; Life Cycle Management (LCM), Business Continuity Management (BCM) – Incident Management (IM), Gifts \& Hospitality (G\&H), Responsible Document Record Management (RDRM), Export Control, SHE, et al.
* This role will also be required to support and conduct any ad\-hoc PM activities required due to the nature of Operations at Dukhan Airbase.


**Requirements**
**Qualifications/Functional Knowledge:**
**Functional Knowledge \& Experience**
* Experienced and in\-depth Project Control knowledge and techniques in an Operational Aircraft Support environment is preferred;
* Experienced resource demand management and forecasting;
* High level of MS Office knowledge and application;
* Programme Reporting experience;
* Understanding and appreciation of operating in a customer\-focused organisation in the Middle East;
* Commercial and Contractual Awareness;
* Purchasing Process and Export control awareness;
* Contract Status Reporting (CSRs).


**Business Expertise**
* Requires good analytical skills, able to manipulate data to identify trends and data shortages. At this level is able to assess if data is complete, accurate and turn into management information for onwards reporting
* Requires the ability to appropriately engage with and challenge a wide range of stakeholders on project performance
* Understands and is able to use and interpret all project management tools sets.
* Requires a good understanding of the work breakdown structure for the service area or project
* Capable of performing detailed performance analysis using a range of PM toolsets and techniques


**Aspirational Experience Of Using The Following Systems**
* JIRA
* Confluence / Tableau


**Qualifications**
* L6 Project Management Degree (complete or in\-progress), or an extensive amount of practical knowledge gained through experience;
* Proficient level of English, written \& verbal.


**Problem Solving**
* High competency in data analysis \& critical thinking
* Ability to challenge and engage at all levels of the business
* Able to perform at both a tactical and strategic level in order to report information appropriately in all settings
* Ability to work under pressure and to timescales;
* Ability to recognise and escalate issues in a timely manner;


**Interpersonal Skills**
* Diplomacy skills required in order to work across business boundaries to achieve optimum solutions;
* Exceptional verbal communication skills across different nationalities;
* Presentation skills for effective reporting against areas of responsibility;
* Strong stakeholder management at various levels of authority both internally and externally and confidence to direct challenge/question all levels of the organisation;
* Time Management skills to effectively discharge work across different areas;
* Confidence to hold/chair meetings \& working groups for associated areas of work;
* A self\-starter.
